Spec: Feature Collector Failure Logging

Purpose:
  Make every fatal collector error visible in job_audit_logs, so that a failed run shows its cause next to the exit code the scheduler writes to system_logs.

Platform: Go/Linux

References:
  ../../../mitm-2.sdd
  ../../../collector-layer/collector-layer.sdd
  ../job-failure-logging/job-failure-logging.sdd

Owns:
  ./**

Can modify:
  /collector-layer/mitm_collector_cdh/main.go
  /collector-layer/mitm_collector_cdh/CHANGELOG.md
  /collector-layer/mitm_collector_csv-xls/main.go
  /collector-layer/mitm_collector_csv-xls/CHANGELOG.md
  /collector-layer/mitm_collector_employee_ora/main.go
  /collector-layer/mitm_collector_employee_ora/CHANGELOG.md
  /collector-layer/mitm_collector_employee_pg/main.go
  /collector-layer/mitm_collector_employee_pg/CHANGELOG.md
  /collector-layer/mitm_collector_kafka/main.go
  /collector-layer/mitm_collector_kafka/CHANGELOG.md
  /collector-layer/mitm_collector_mft/main.go
  /collector-layer/mitm_collector_mft/CHANGELOG.md
  /collector-layer/mitm_collector_ora/main.go
  /collector-layer/mitm_collector_ora/CHANGELOG.md
  /collector-layer/mitm_collector_pg/main.go
  /collector-layer/mitm_collector_pg/CHANGELOG.md
  /CHANGELOG.md

Must:
  Every fatal error of a collector sends the `failed` status event and the audit event `ERROR: <message>` to the scheduler and then exits with code 1, using one fatal helper per collector.
  Unparsable collector arguments (JSON in `os.Args[1]`) are a fatal error; a collector must not continue with default values.
  mitm_collector_mft checks every cipher initialization and the minimum length of the wrapped DEK instead of panicking.
  mitm_collector_cdh sends the actual error message instead of a generic text.

Must not:
  Send secrets (passwords, client secrets, access tokens, Master Key, decrypted payloads or source configurations) in status or audit events.
  Change the behavior of a collector on successful runs.

Tasks:
  [x] #1 mitm_collector_ora and mitm_collector_employee_ora: fatal helper for all fatal errors, abort on unparsable arguments.
  [x] #2 mitm_collector_pg and mitm_collector_employee_pg: fatal helper for all fatal errors, abort on unparsable arguments.
  [x] #3 mitm_collector_kafka: fatal helper for all fatal errors, abort on unparsable arguments.
  [x] #4 mitm_collector_mft: fatal helper for all fatal errors, abort on unparsable arguments, error checks instead of panics.
  [x] #5 mitm_collector_csv-xls: use the existing fatal helper for the remaining fatal errors.
  [x] #6 mitm_collector_cdh: report the actual error, also for invalid job arguments.
  [x] #7 Update versions and CHANGELOGs; add a CHANGELOG to mitm_collector_cdh.

Done when:
  `go vet`, `go build` and `go test` succeed for every collector, and a failing run of each collector shows its error in job_audit_logs.

Scenario: unparsable collector arguments
  Given the job arguments are not valid JSON
  When the scheduler runs any collector job
  Then the collector exits with code 1
  And job_audit_logs contains `ERROR: ...` with the parse error for the run

Scenario: source credentials missing
  Given there is no active `source_credentials` entry for the configured source
  When the scheduler runs any collector job
  Then the collector exits with code 1
  And job_audit_logs contains `ERROR: ...` naming the failed credential lookup for the run
